    "standardized_narrative": "The syndicate's opening gross claims reserves at 1 January 2021 were GBP 355.5m. Using the gross claims development (claims triangle) the syndicate experienced a net gross prior-year strengthening of approximately GBP 30.8m (c.8.7% of opening reserves) driven largely by adverse re-estimation in the 2019 underwriting year that outweighed releases in older years. The report cites a mix of higher-than-expected incurred movements across multiple lines, the impact of various natural catastrophe events and ongoing COVID-19 related uncertainty as primary drivers. Older back years (2018 and prior) produced some releases, but these were more than offset by deterioration concentrated in the more recent (pre-2020) years.",
    "raw_causal_phrases": [
      "In 2021, there has been an overall net (deficit) / surplus in ultimate claims of GBP (8.7m) (2020: GBP 6.0m) due to (higher) / lower than expected incurred movements across most classes of business.",
      "The back years, 2018 and prior, contributed GBP 20.6m to the annual result, following better than expected reserve utilisation in the calendar year.",
      "A positive run-off of GBP 18.5m on the 2018 and prior years' reserves (2017 and prior: GBP 16.1m) was experienced in the year."
